{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"64beaa93-65a4-45d6-8fbd-d2b228b5137c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The issue was caused by [`display_date`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-without/repo/journal.py#L33) in [journal.py](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-without/repo/journal.py):\n\n- When rendering a post card, `display_date` parsed `post[\"date\"]` (the server's UTC date) and anchored it at noon UTC (`+ \"T12:00:00+00:00\"`), intentionally suppressing calendar day rollovers.\n- Because it ignored the actual creation timestamp (`post[\"created_at\"]`), posts published across midnight boundaries in different time zones displayed the UTC date instead of the viewer's local calendar date.\n\n### Changes Made\n\n1. **[journal.py](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-without/repo/journal.py#L33-L44)**:\n   - Updated [`display_date`](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-without/repo/journal.py#L33) to convert `post[\"created_at\"]` to the requested `viewer_tz` using `ZoneInfo(viewer_tz)`.\n\n2. **[tests/test_journal.py](file:///private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-valentinakoniukhova-projects-worklore/3bfdd3c9-cfe2-4fd1-a8b7-ce52b613a3aa/scratchpad/story-eval/runs/s3-agy-flash-without/repo/tests/test_journal.py#L38-L58)**:\n   - Added test cases covering posts created across midnight in different time zones (`Europe/Berlin` late night, `America/Los_Angeles` evening, and `Asia/Tokyo` morning).\n\nAll tests run and pass with `python3 -m unittest discover -s tests`.\n","duration_seconds":275.297981,"num_tu